We can still remove the copy-paste like this: https://github.com/ASverdlov/kubernetes/commit/675e411ae6958bc6b07e7ae104480e316e403fd4.

Attempt on a clear comment on why it would work follows: let's compare 2 versions:
```go
	cronJobCopy, requeueAfter, updateStatus, err := jm.syncCronJob(ctx, cronJob, jobsToBeReconciled)
	if err != nil {
		logger.V(2).Info("Error reconciling cronjob", "cronjob", klog.KObj(cronJob), "err", err)

                COPY_PASTE()
		return nil, err
	}

        COPY_PASTE()

	if requeueAfter != nil {
		logger.V(4).Info("Re-queuing cronjob", "cronjob", klog.KObj(cronJob), "requeueAfter", requeueAfter)
		return requeueAfter, nil
	}
	// this marks the key done, currently only happens when the cronjob is suspended or spec has invalid schedule format
	return nil, nil

```
and

```go
	cronJobCopy, requeueAfter, updateStatus, reconciliationErr := jm.syncCronJob(ctx, cronJob, jobsToBeReconciled)
	if err != nil {
		logger.V(2).Info("Error reconciling cronjob", "cronjob", klog.KObj(cronJob), "err", err)
	}
        
        COPY_PASTE()

	if requeueAfter != nil {
		logger.V(4).Info("Re-queuing cronjob", "cronjob", klog.KObj(cronJob), "requeueAfter", requeueAfter)
		return requeueAfter, reconciliationErr
	}
	// this marks the key done, currently only happens when the cronjob is suspended or spec has invalid schedule format
	return nil, reconciliationErr

```

* In case `jm.syncCronJob` doesn't return an error, they are line-by-line the same (if you ignore renaming of the error variable.
* In case `jm.syncCronJob` does return an error, the only difference is: latter code also returns a `requeueAfter` in case it was set. But `jm.syncCronJob()` never returns a `requeueAfter != nil` when it returns an error, so in practice it doesn't change the current behaviour.

I was actually looking at the 2nd proposal from the above, iow.:
1. move cleaning before sync, since we always want to clean the finished jobs based on settings
2. invoke update only once.

In short I was thinking of replacing this whole block https://github.com/kubernetes/kubernetes/blob/7bde29372ad36a8fe7a78f956c5754c5a62f1a33/pkg/controller/cronjob/cronjob_controllerv2.go#L199-L221 with something like the above:
```golang
	updateStatus := false
	if jm.cleanupFinishedJobs(ctx, cronJob, jobsToBeReconciled) {
		updateStatus = true
	}

	cronJobCopy, requeueAfter, updateStatus, syncErr := jm.syncCronJob(ctx, cronJob, jobsToBeReconciled)
	if syncErr != nil {
		logger.V(2).Info("Error reconciling cronjob", "cronjob", klog.KObj(cronJob), "err", syncErr)
	}
	if updateStatus {
		if _, err := jm.cronJobControl.UpdateStatus(ctx, cronJobCopy); err != nil {
			logger.V(2).Info("Unable to update status for cronjob", "cronjob", klog.KObj(cronJob), "resourceVersion", cronJob.ResourceVersion, "err", err)
			return nil, err
		}
	}
	if syncErr != nil {
		return nil, syncErr
	}
```
This would ensure cleaning happens always, and we don't have duplicated code. @ASverdlov opinions?
